1
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:11,767
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,633 --> 00:00:32,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:35,133
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,200
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,033
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:45,000
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,233
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:51,200
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,600
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:55,433
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,733 --> 00:00:57,467
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,067
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:09,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,667
- [GUNSHOT
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:12,200
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:14,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:24,433
<i>I'm just worried about Sam.
The NCIA investigates her today.</i>

21
00:01:24,567 --> 00:01:25,667
<i> In our line of work, Ma,</i>

22
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,533
<i>all of our actions
have consequences.</i>

23
00:01:27,667 --> 00:01:30,033
<i>It's either a reward
or a punishment.</i>

24
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,600
<i> Well, Samantha?!</i>

25
00:01:33,233 --> 00:01:35,167
<i>We'll act like
we're Django's crew.</i>

26
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,667
<i> We've got to convince him.</i>

27
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:39,100
<i>- Hey! I knew it!
- What are you talking about?</i>

28
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:40,633
<i> He told us to spy on you.</i>

29
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,533
<i>Django thinks
we're his men again.</i>

30
00:01:43,667 --> 00:01:45,633
<i>Make Django believe
you're on his side.</i>

31
00:01:45,767 --> 00:01:47,700
<i>You'll be my eyes and ears
in their group.</i>

32
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:51,000
<i>Why is your wound that bad?
It's swelling and bruising!</i>

33
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:54,167
<i>I didn't buy my medicine.
I gambled and lost the money.</i>

34
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:55,167
<i>Papa used the money
for gambling?</i>

35
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,500
<i> I was just hopeful.</i>

36
00:01:57,633 --> 00:01:59,267
<i>You saw how hard I worked
for that money.</i>

37
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,333
But you just used it to gamble?!

38
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:01,767
<i> Son, I'm sorry.</i>

39
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:04,367
So, Betchay?

40
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,233
Have you thought about my offer?

41
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,833
I'll have to decline.

42
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:15,200
I discovered a new gig today.

43
00:02:15,367 --> 00:02:16,733
- Hm.
- But don't worry!

44
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:19,833
If I need money again,
I'll come to you!

45
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:20,800
[PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

46
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:23,200
[ROMY] But you seem
to be enjoying here.

47
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:24,467
Of course!

48
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,500
I'm even having fun
talking to those guys.

49
00:02:28,867 --> 00:02:29,567
[BOTTLES CLINK]

50
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,367
- Let's do it this way.
- Hm?

51
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,600
Why don't you manage BeerGin?

52
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:37,400
Really?

53
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:43,233
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

54
00:02:43,367 --> 00:02:46,433
After all, you already know
how to run this,

55
00:02:46,567 --> 00:02:49,900
and how
to make it profitable. Right?

56
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,300
But if I manage this...

57
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:55,367
[WHISPERING] I'll replace
your girls.

58
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,433
Oh, no! Don't!

59
00:02:56,567 --> 00:02:59,667
They've been working here
for a long time!

60
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:08,167
But Betchay...

61
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:11,900
You're the one
who brings the energy

62
00:03:12,033 --> 00:03:14,467
and the money to BeerGin.

63
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:19,367
And, as the owner,
I think I have the right...

64
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:23,333
...to offer you
to manage BeerGin.

65
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,933
Well?

66
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:29,067
Do you accept?

67
00:03:33,667 --> 00:03:36,367
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

68
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,567
- Alright, I accept.
- Hah!

69
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:43,067
I'll plan a gimmick
to make BeerGin popular again!

70
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:46,000
- When do I start?
- If you want...

71
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:47,967
...right now!

72
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,733
- Now? Really?
- Yeah! Yes!

73
00:03:51,967 --> 00:03:52,867
[BOTTLES CLINK]

74
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:54,800
- [BOTTLES CLINK]
- That's it!

75
00:03:54,967 --> 00:04:01,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

76
00:04:03,367 --> 00:04:08,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

77
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,333
[CAR DOORS OPENING]

78
00:04:10,467 --> 00:04:15,767
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

79
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:16,867
Sam!

80
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:18,467
Check out everything, Rallos.

81
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,733
- Yes, sir!
- Sam!

82
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:26,567
Here, here, here!

83
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,033
Her cellphone.

84
00:04:30,467 --> 00:04:37,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

85
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,200
- Sam!
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]

86
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:47,300
- Sam!
- Sam isn't here.

87
00:04:47,433 --> 00:04:49,233
We should go to General Jacinto.

88
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:52,967
But, sir,
Sam might be in danger.

89
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,333
The people who ambushed her
might've taken her.

90
00:04:54,467 --> 00:04:56,067
Can we look for her first?

91
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,067
[SEBASTIAN SIGHS]

92
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:57,900
[PHONE RINGING]

93
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:01,500
- Castor.
- Sir Seb, we're close.

94
00:05:01,667 --> 00:05:03,333
Sam isn't here
in the nearby area.

95
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:05,367
We'll go to General Jacinto.

96
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,800
I want you
to continue investigating here.

97
00:05:06,933 --> 00:05:08,400
Okay, sir.
We'll take care of it.

98
00:05:09,233 --> 00:05:10,167
Come on, let's go.

99
00:05:14,267 --> 00:05:15,733
[DOOR OPENS]

100
00:05:15,867 --> 00:05:18,367
Sir, Ma'am, you called for me?

101
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:05:21,033 --> 00:05:23,667
Any updates from Lucas
or his men?

103
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,167
The last thing Lao told me was

104
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,533
they were following
Samantha Jacinto.

105
00:05:27,667 --> 00:05:29,467
[DEBORAH] Yeah,
but how long ago was that?

106
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:33,633
Why haven't we received
any updates?

107
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,200
That's just a feeble woman.

108
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:37,933
Taking her down should be easy.

109
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:42,467
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

110
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,467
[FOOTSTEPS RUNNING]

111
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:49,967
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

112
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,600
[PHONE RINGING]

113
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,033
Hello, Ma.

114
00:05:55,167 --> 00:05:56,367
Lucas, where are you?

115
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,333
We're here at First Creek.

116
00:05:58,467 --> 00:06:00,633
What are you doing there?

117
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:02,267
What happened
to the original plan?

118
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,967
We got her.

119
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:06,067
Where's Samantha?

120
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,633
We opened fire in her direction.

121
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,400
We got her
and she fell into the river.

122
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:10,667
Is she dead?

123
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:14,633
Pa, with how many bullets
we fired, for sure she's dead.

124
00:06:14,767 --> 00:06:16,333
Did you see it
with your own eyes?

125
00:06:16,467 --> 00:06:17,367
<i> Where is the body?</i>

126
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,033
We haven't seen the body.

127
00:06:19,167 --> 00:06:21,067
<i> I used to be a cop, Lucas.</i>

128
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:24,000
The most important lesson
I have learned is that,

129
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,600
if there is no body,
death is not a certainty.

130
00:06:26,733 --> 00:06:31,300
So don't come back here
until you confirm she's dead!

131
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:33,233
<i>- Do your job properly.
- Yes, Pa.</i>

132
00:06:36,233 --> 00:06:36,400
Lao.

133
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:38,533
Lee.

134
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,233
[MUSIC FADES]

135
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:45,033
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:06:45,167 --> 00:06:48,067
[CAR APPROACHING]

137
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,633
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

138
00:06:53,067 --> 00:06:54,767
What are you doing?!
Get out of here!

139
00:06:59,933 --> 00:07:02,767
Team, check the area
if there's someone alive!

140
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:05,367
But don't touch the bodies.

141
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,300
Bullet, secure the perimeter.

142
00:07:07,433 --> 00:07:08,600
Copy. On it.

143
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,233
James, call the forensic team.

144
00:07:12,367 --> 00:07:12,900
Okay.

145
00:07:14,667 --> 00:07:15,700
[PHONE DIAL TONE BEEPS]

146
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:17,533
Robert, check if there's a CCTV
in the area.

147
00:07:26,133 --> 00:07:28,600
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

148
00:07:31,067 --> 00:07:33,000
- Yes.
- Sir.

149
00:07:33,133 --> 00:07:34,200
How's everything?

150
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,167
Did you see her?

151
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,867
Sir, we found the car
here on Soriano Street.

152
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,633
It has multiple gunshots.

153
00:07:42,667 --> 00:07:44,367
There are casualties as well.

154
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,567
But, sir...

155
00:07:46,667 --> 00:07:48,100
Sam is not here.

156
00:07:48,267 --> 00:07:49,633
What?!

157
00:07:49,767 --> 00:07:51,567
Find out what happened
and where Sam is.

158
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,367
We need to be sure
that she is safe.

159
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:56,567
Yes, sir.

160
00:08:00,567 --> 00:08:02,567
[CAR APPROACHING]

161
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:05,300
[CAR DOORS OPEN]

162
00:08:05,433 --> 00:08:06,733
[CAR DOORS CLOSE]

163
00:08:06,867 --> 00:08:07,467
Is General Jacinto in there?

164
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:10,867
You are from NCIA, right?

165
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:11,733
He's inside.

166
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:15,167
Oh, Sir Handsome,
where's Ma'am Sam?

167
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:15,700
That's what we came here for.

168
00:08:17,533 --> 00:08:18,900
Why?

169
00:08:19,033 --> 00:08:20,867
We need to talk
to General about something.

170
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:24,100
Come on. Come on in.

171
00:08:26,767 --> 00:08:28,600
You'd better get some rest, Ma.

172
00:08:28,733 --> 00:08:32,000
Oh, see? They took her home.

173
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:34,067
- See? I told you.
- Ma'am.

174
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,133
- Oh, Sebastian.
- Ma'am, you have guests.

175
00:08:36,267 --> 00:08:39,733
Auntie, we're sorry
for coming here so late.

176
00:08:39,867 --> 00:08:42,333
Yes. Where's Sam?
Where's Sam?

177
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,167
Is General Jacinto home?

178
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:46,567
There is something important
you need to know.

179
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:48,700
- Huh?
- What happened?

180
00:08:48,833 --> 00:08:50,767
- What are you doing here?
- Sir.

181
00:08:53,267 --> 00:08:55,367
Please stay calm.

182
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,867
Someone ambushed Sam.

183
00:08:59,733 --> 00:09:01,600
We didn't know
where she is right now

184
00:09:01,733 --> 00:09:03,667
and we saw her car
riddled with bullets.

185
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:08,267
What?! My daughter was shot!
God! [SOBBING]

186
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,667
Ma'am, we're doing everything
to find her.

187
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:14,067
Our team is still searching
the area.

188
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,800
Where did you last see
Sam's car?

189
00:09:15,933 --> 00:09:17,400
At Soriano Street.

190
00:09:17,533 --> 00:09:19,967
- Ricardo, our daughter!
- Isobel.

191
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,667
- Our daughter!
- I'll fix this.

192
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:39,100
- [METAL ROOF RATTLES]
- [DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]

193
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,867
- Rosanna.
- Mmm, boss?

194
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,833
From now on,

195
00:09:50,067 --> 00:09:53,133
Betchay will be
the manager of BeerGin.

196
00:09:53,267 --> 00:09:55,167
What? Why her?

197
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:55,700
Because I said so!

198
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:58,467
Whatever she says,

199
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,600
that's what you'll do.

200
00:10:00,733 --> 00:10:03,367
No, no, no.
Wait a minute, boss.

201
00:10:03,533 --> 00:10:05,700
I've been a manager here
for a long time!

202
00:10:05,833 --> 00:10:06,367
Let me remind you, boss...

203
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,200
We used to own this bar!

204
00:10:09,333 --> 00:10:11,100
That was then, but not now!

205
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:12,967
[PAQUITO] Rosanna...

206
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,233
You seem to forget one thing.

207
00:10:15,367 --> 00:10:18,467
Back then, because of how big
your debt was to me,

208
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:22,400
you used BeerGin
to pay it all off!

209
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,533
So you're the forgetful one,
Rosanna.

210
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:25,600
Don't get on my nerves, Betchay!

211
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:30,267
You're lucky
I haven't fired you,

212
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:32,733
even with BeerGin losing
so much money!

213
00:10:32,867 --> 00:10:34,367
I'll bring back the charm
of BeerGin!

214
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,367
Leave it to me!

215
00:10:36,533 --> 00:10:38,333
- Don't annoy me!
- Now, now...

216
00:10:38,467 --> 00:10:39,467
Listen up.

217
00:10:40,167 --> 00:10:43,000
If you're not happy
with Betchay,

218
00:10:43,133 --> 00:10:45,133
- then pack your bags...
- [ROSANNA] What?!

219
00:10:45,267 --> 00:10:47,433
and look for another job!

220
00:10:47,567 --> 00:10:49,133
- [PRISCILLA] Come on, boss...
- My goodness.

221
00:10:50,867 --> 00:10:52,233
- Betchay.
- You witch--

222
00:10:52,367 --> 00:10:53,400
- [PAQUITO] Let's go.
- You're going to regret this!

223
00:10:53,533 --> 00:10:55,400
How dare you!

224
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,433
- Did you all see that?
- The nerve!

225
00:10:57,567 --> 00:11:00,033
She's new here,
and already a manager!

226
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:01,400
Mark my words, Priscilla.

227
00:11:01,533 --> 00:11:03,233
I'll make her life miserable.

228
00:11:03,367 --> 00:11:04,367
And that's how it should be!

229
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:08,767
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:11:08,933 --> 00:11:10,867
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

231
00:11:11,567 --> 00:11:12,967
Sir, is it true?

232
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:14,967
That Jacinto...

233
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,400
[DELGADO] Sam was ambushed.

234
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:20,000
Until now,
she still hasn't been found.

235
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,267
Do you think she was kidnapped?

236
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,400
Abducted?

237
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:26,567
Or maybe she's just in hiding,
she ran away on purpose,

238
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,633
because she's avoiding her case.

239
00:11:28,767 --> 00:11:30,433
[DELGADO] Pia...

240
00:11:30,567 --> 00:11:34,333
Her car was riddled
with bullets.

241
00:11:34,933 --> 00:11:36,033
Oh my!

242
00:11:36,767 --> 00:11:38,767
Poor thing...

243
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:40,467
Full of bullet holes?

244
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,800
Do you think she's still alive?

245
00:11:42,967 --> 00:11:46,167
To date, no body
has been recovered.

246
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,400
Hmm.

247
00:11:47,533 --> 00:11:48,900
[INHALES DEEPLY]

248
00:11:49,033 --> 00:11:52,433
Well, is there already
a prime suspect?

249
00:11:52,867 --> 00:11:54,600
None other than the Zafras.

250
00:11:54,733 --> 00:11:58,667
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:02,333
First, it was Mr. Chan
and Team Bravo.

252
00:12:02,467 --> 00:12:03,700
Now, it's Sam.

253
00:12:03,833 --> 00:12:07,967
They were all involved
in Victor Zafra's case.

254
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:09,967
[INHALES DEEPLY]

255
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,267
[CLEARS THROAT]

256
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:12,867
So, what now?

257
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:16,467
We have no witnesses.

258
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,833
And on top of that,
Jacinto is missing.

259
00:12:18,967 --> 00:12:20,733
So how will the case proceed?

260
00:12:20,867 --> 00:12:27,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

261
00:12:32,233 --> 00:12:32,667
[MUSIC FADES]

262
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,500
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:12:34,633 --> 00:12:35,900
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

264
00:12:36,833 --> 00:12:38,100
[DOOR OPENS]

265
00:12:41,533 --> 00:12:42,633
- [LOUD THUD]
- [CHAIR SCRAPING]

266
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:45,100
[DELGADO] Three tragedies...

267
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:47,567
They all occurred
in a short period of time

268
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,767
after your parents came
to visit.

269
00:12:49,933 --> 00:12:51,867
Mr. Chan's convoy was ambushed.

270
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,567
And now, the same thing
happened to Agent Jacinto!

271
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:58,533
Admit that you have
something to do with it.

272
00:12:58,667 --> 00:13:01,000
Admit that your family
is involved.

273
00:13:01,133 --> 00:13:02,367
I don't know.

274
00:13:02,967 --> 00:13:04,233
You're the investigator,
remember?

275
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:06,267
Why don't you look
for evidence yourself?

276
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,067
Don't be sarcastic with me.

277
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:11,500
We're talking about the life
of my agent here!

278
00:13:11,633 --> 00:13:13,633
If your agents
are getting killed,

279
00:13:13,767 --> 00:13:15,633
don't try to pin the blame
on others!

280
00:13:15,767 --> 00:13:16,700
[BLOW LANDS]

281
00:13:16,833 --> 00:13:17,867
- Sir!
- That's enough, sir!

282
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,233
- [DELGADO] Let me go!
- Sir!

283
00:13:19,367 --> 00:13:20,700
- Stop this, sir!
- Get your hands off me!

284
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:22,733
- Sir!
- [DELGADO] Victor!

285
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:26,567
I get now why
Jacinto punched Mr. Chan.

286
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:27,867
Because she learned it from you!

287
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,533
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:13:29,667 --> 00:13:30,267
[DELGADO] Don't touch me!

289
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,900
- Sir!
- Just let me--

290
00:13:32,033 --> 00:13:33,067
- Sir! Sir!
- I said--

291
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,667
Leave me alone!

292
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,533
Stay out of this!

293
00:13:36,667 --> 00:13:43,200
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

294
00:13:43,333 --> 00:13:44,300
Well?

295
00:13:44,433 --> 00:13:45,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

296
00:13:45,567 --> 00:13:46,100
Can you do it?

297
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,867
Then pull the trigger!

298
00:13:57,467 --> 00:13:59,100
Listen very carefully.

299
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:05,767
If I prove you and your family
are behind all this,

300
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:07,767
I won't just let you rot
in prison.

301
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,367
I'll destroy your organization!

302
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:16,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

303
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:22,833
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

304
00:14:24,833 --> 00:14:26,100
Now...

305
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:28,167
Get him out of here!

306
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:38,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,033
[GATE HANDLE CLANKING]

308
00:14:52,867 --> 00:14:55,967
[VICTOR]
You survived after all, Jacinto.

309
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,933
<i> But it's not your time yet.</i>

310
00:14:58,067 --> 00:14:59,967
<i>Because I'll be the one
to end you</i>

311
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:00,767
<i> when the moment is right!</i>

312
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,867
<i> I'm going to make you pay,</i>

313
00:15:03,033 --> 00:15:06,633
<i>as well as the man responsible
for my imprisonment!</i>

314
00:15:06,767 --> 00:15:13,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:15:18,033 --> 00:15:21,567
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

316
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:23,367
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

317
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:33,667
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" BY
JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

318
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,267
[GABO] Papa is right.

319
00:15:36,433 --> 00:15:38,133
<i> I am getting older.</i>

320
00:15:38,267 --> 00:15:39,467
<i> And yet...</i>

321
00:15:40,267 --> 00:15:41,933
<i>my life still doesn't have
a clear direction.</i>

322
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:49,000
<i>Hopefully, this job will be
the start of a better life.</i>

323
00:15:49,133 --> 00:15:51,800
<i> For me and for my family.</i>

324
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:56,100
<i>I just pray nothing bad
happens to me.</i>

325
00:15:56,233 --> 00:15:58,833
<i> I don't know any other job.</i>

326
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:02,167
<i>I didn't finish school,
after all.</i>

327
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:04,467
<i>The only good thing
I've ever been good at</i>

328
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,700
<i> is throwing punches.</i>

329
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:10,900
<i> So this is what I'll do,
</i>to give my life some direction.

330
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,667
<i> In all honesty,</i>

331
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:15,133
<i> I'm not asking for too much.</i>

332
00:16:15,267 --> 00:16:17,700
<i>I'm already content
with the way we live now.</i>

333
00:16:18,233 --> 00:16:20,433
<i> We get by, one day at a time.</i>

334
00:16:21,033 --> 00:16:24,533
<i>Maybe the only thing
I'm missing...</i>

335
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:29,100
<i>is a woman I can love
and spend my life with.</i>

336
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:30,967
<i> Lord,</i>

337
00:16:31,767 --> 00:16:33,867
<i>I'm not asking for someone
extraordinarily beautiful.</i>

338
00:16:35,233 --> 00:16:37,533
<i>I'd be happy
with someone simple,</i>

339
00:16:37,667 --> 00:16:40,367
<i>as long as she cares for me
and loves me.</i>

340
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:43,233
I hope she'll love our children
<i> the same way.</i>

341
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:44,900
<i>I pray she comes
into my life soon, Lord.</i>

342
00:16:46,267 --> 00:16:48,100
<i> I pray I finally meet her.</i>

343
00:16:48,233 --> 00:16:48,867
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

344
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,067
I'm ready, Lord.

345
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:52,967
You can drop her to me
if You want to.

346
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:56,433
- [CRASHING]
- [SCREAMING]

347
00:16:56,567 --> 00:16:58,267
Oh! Oh!

348
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:01,200
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

349
00:17:03,767 --> 00:17:09,000
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

350
00:17:09,133 --> 00:17:11,267
Lord, that was quick!

351
00:17:20,433 --> 00:17:21,867
What was that?!

352
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:22,900
[MAMENG, RUDY GASP]

353
00:17:23,033 --> 00:17:25,267
Gabo! Who is that?!
Where did she come from?!

354
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:27,633
[RUDY] What the...

355
00:17:27,767 --> 00:17:28,567
[GRUNTS]

356
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:31,267
And why does she have a gun?!

357
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:34,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

358
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,767
I-I don't know, Pa.

359
00:17:41,067 --> 00:17:42,000
Miss?

360
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:44,900
Miss? Miss?

361
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:55,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

362
00:17:55,233 --> 00:17:58,167
Pa, I know this woman!

363
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,933
We've crossed paths many times!

364
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,033
She's an NCIA agent!

365
00:18:04,167 --> 00:18:05,800
What?!
She works for the NCIA?!

366
00:18:05,933 --> 00:18:07,800
Why is there an
NCIA agent in my home?!

367
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:08,967
Wait a minute!

368
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:09,967
Did she fall down
from the roof?

369
00:18:10,133 --> 00:18:10,500
Yes!

370
00:18:11,233 --> 00:18:13,267
I don't know, Pa.

371
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:16,267
I remember I was praying,

372
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,300
"Lord, give me
the woman of my dreams!"

373
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:21,567
Then she just
came out of nowhere!

374
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,900
How did this happen?

375
00:18:24,133 --> 00:18:27,600
What's all this ruckus?

376
00:18:27,733 --> 00:18:29,067
Who is that?

377
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:34,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:40,300
- Hey, Paquito.
- Hmm?

379
00:18:40,433 --> 00:18:43,267
The ACs aren't working properly,
and they reek of mold.

380
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:45,067
We should have them cleaned.

381
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,033
Romy, have the ACs fixed.

382
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:49,467
And this too.

383
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:52,100
The songs in the karaoke
are all outdated.

384
00:18:52,233 --> 00:18:56,067
Romy, have them replace
the karaoke machines.

385
00:18:56,233 --> 00:18:58,400
Wait, I just sat down.
Take it easy.

386
00:18:58,533 --> 00:19:01,967
- Hello there.
- Oh, hi!

387
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,800
Kulas!
What are you doing here?

388
00:19:04,933 --> 00:19:06,033
Keep it down, Betchay.

389
00:19:06,167 --> 00:19:07,633
Oh, sorry.

390
00:19:07,767 --> 00:19:10,800
Don't worry.
I'm the new manager here.

391
00:19:10,933 --> 00:19:12,100
I'll give you a table.

392
00:19:12,233 --> 00:19:14,433
Who do you want
to keep you company?

393
00:19:14,567 --> 00:19:16,100
- Come with me.
- Oh, Betchay! Betchay!

394
00:19:16,233 --> 00:19:18,133
- Hmm?
- That's Aya's regular customer.

395
00:19:18,267 --> 00:19:20,533
- Him?
- That's right.

396
00:19:20,667 --> 00:19:23,400
You're a regular customer here?

397
00:19:23,533 --> 00:19:26,167
After all those horrible things
your wife said about me!

398
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:28,100
Sorry about Diday, Betchay.

399
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:30,133
Oh, don't worry.
Where's Aya?

400
00:19:30,267 --> 00:19:32,600
- Aya!
- Where are you? Come here!

401
00:19:32,733 --> 00:19:34,767
- Your regular's here.
- You sly fox. [CHUCKLES]

402
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:38,167
Oh, it's been a while
since I last saw you!

403
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:39,700
- I missed you.
- [AYA EXCLAIMS]

404
00:19:39,833 --> 00:19:41,133
[CHUCKLES]
Have a seat. Go ahead.

405
00:19:41,267 --> 00:19:44,467
Betchay, could you
keep me company tonight?

406
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:47,367
Oh, Kanor.
I don't do that anymore.

407
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:49,267
I'm the manager now.

408
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,133
But I can give you
one of our best girls.

409
00:19:51,267 --> 00:19:53,100
- What? Me?
- Yes, that's right.

410
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:55,933
- She's the best!
- Alright!

411
00:19:56,067 --> 00:19:58,200
- Hey! Take their order!
- Waitress! I'd like to order!

412
00:19:58,333 --> 00:20:01,867
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

413
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:04,567
Ma'am.

414
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:06,467
She's here.

415
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:13,667
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

416
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,033
You're late.

417
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:26,067
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

418
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,033
Oh, we have company this late?

419
00:20:32,133 --> 00:20:33,467
This is Pia.

420
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:36,700
Wait a minute.

421
00:20:37,333 --> 00:20:39,767
You're from the NCIA.

422
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:42,533
You helped us when
Delgado cornered us.

423
00:20:42,667 --> 00:20:43,567
Yes.

424
00:20:44,433 --> 00:20:48,667
And that's not all
I can do for you.

425
00:20:49,533 --> 00:20:51,533
Why didn't you tell me

426
00:20:51,667 --> 00:20:53,367
we had a connection
within the NCIA?

427
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:57,767
I didn't want to tell you
until it was for sure.

428
00:20:59,867 --> 00:21:04,533
We sealed the deal
just recently, right, Pia?

429
00:21:04,667 --> 00:21:06,333
Right.

430
00:21:06,467 --> 00:21:08,100
When Victor was caught,

431
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:10,400
I did my homework.

432
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,033
<i>Thank you for
agreeing to meet me.</i>

433
00:21:17,167 --> 00:21:18,767
<i> Cut to the chase.</i>

434
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:21,233
<i>Is this about your son
in NCIA custody?</i>

435
00:21:21,367 --> 00:21:24,033
I just want to get to know you.

436
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:25,400
<i> Establish a connection.</i>

437
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:27,433
<i> Maybe one day,</i>

438
00:21:27,567 --> 00:21:29,967
<i> a possible partnership.</i>

439
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,467
<i> A collaboration?</i>

440
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,000
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

441
00:21:35,967 --> 00:21:37,233
<i> I know people like you.</i>

442
00:21:37,367 --> 00:21:41,233
<i> And I know your tactics.</i>

443
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,200
[SCOFFS]

444
00:21:42,333 --> 00:21:44,533
<i> I'm sure that</i>

445
00:21:44,667 --> 00:21:47,833
<i>after all these years
with the NCIA,</i>

446
00:21:48,567 --> 00:21:50,867
<i> you know a lot.</i>

447
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,667
<i> But in the real world,</i>

448
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:56,167
<i> it's not what you know,</i>

449
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,967
<i> but who you know that matters.</i>

450
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:06,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

451
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:26,200
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:30,000
So we have a mole
in the NCIA now.

453
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:31,433
A mole?

454
00:22:31,567 --> 00:22:35,967
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

455
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,733
I am not your mole.

456
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:43,633
I am your asset.

457
00:22:49,233 --> 00:22:51,700
- Betchay.
- Yes, boss?

458
00:22:51,833 --> 00:22:52,900
Come here.

459
00:22:54,333 --> 00:22:55,800
- Here.
- Oh...

460
00:22:55,933 --> 00:22:59,100
Crispy pork leg
and stir-fried noodles.

461
00:22:59,233 --> 00:23:00,533
[BETCHAY] Huh?

462
00:23:00,667 --> 00:23:02,767
[PAQUITO] Bring it home.

463
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:05,367
Gabo and Rudy can eat them.

464
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:09,400
Do you want them to eat these
because you put poison in them?

465
00:23:09,533 --> 00:23:11,033
Of course not.

466
00:23:11,167 --> 00:23:12,600
I bought those for you.

467
00:23:12,733 --> 00:23:15,033
Just give them some.

468
00:23:15,167 --> 00:23:16,300
Will these be deducted
from my next paycheck?

469
00:23:16,433 --> 00:23:18,900
Nope.

470
00:23:19,033 --> 00:23:20,467
Consider a bonus

471
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:24,267
for being a good manager.

472
00:23:24,433 --> 00:23:25,867
Wow!

473
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:30,833
So this is what it feels like
to be appreciated.

474
00:23:30,967 --> 00:23:33,933
- Thanks, boss!
- [PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

475
00:23:34,067 --> 00:23:35,400
You know, Betchay,

476
00:23:35,533 --> 00:23:40,833
if you chose me
back in the day,

477
00:23:40,967 --> 00:23:44,233
you wouldn't just be
getting food.

478
00:23:44,367 --> 00:23:45,567
[ROMY] That's right!

479
00:23:46,767 --> 00:23:48,267
[LIPS SMACKS, CHUCKLES]

480
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:49,567
Alright.

481
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:50,767
[ROSANNA] Bye, boss.

482
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:53,800
- Bye-bye!
- Take care, boss.

483
00:23:53,933 --> 00:23:54,833
Alright.

484
00:23:56,367 --> 00:24:00,767
No wonder she became manager.

485
00:24:00,900 --> 00:24:03,167
She's flirting with the boss.

486
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:04,100
That's why.

487
00:24:04,233 --> 00:24:08,100
No wonder Ibyang was replaced.

488
00:24:08,233 --> 00:24:10,400
But what about Rudy?

489
00:24:10,533 --> 00:24:12,400
Didn't he just
get out of the hospital?

490
00:24:12,533 --> 00:24:15,400
- Yes.
- I'm not worried about Rudy.

491
00:24:15,533 --> 00:24:18,967
What if Ibyang finds out?

492
00:24:19,733 --> 00:24:21,067
Are you going to tell her?

493
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:26,667
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

494
00:24:29,633 --> 00:24:30,767
[GABO] Miss?

495
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:32,600
Miss.

496
00:24:32,733 --> 00:24:34,000
I don't know!

497
00:24:34,133 --> 00:24:40,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

498
00:24:41,100 --> 00:24:42,233
Gabo.

499
00:24:45,833 --> 00:24:51,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

500
00:24:51,333 --> 00:24:51,667
- Pa!
- What?

501
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,700
She's injured.

502
00:24:53,833 --> 00:24:55,133
- Oh, dear.
- She's injured.

503
00:24:55,267 --> 00:24:57,167
Oh, Gabo!

504
00:24:57,300 --> 00:24:59,433
Get some medicine!

505
00:24:59,567 --> 00:25:00,433
I'll take care of her wounds.

506
00:25:00,567 --> 00:25:03,467
Then get her something to wear

507
00:25:03,633 --> 00:25:06,333
so I can change her clothes.

508
00:25:06,467 --> 00:25:10,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

509
00:25:10,500 --> 00:25:12,800
Go on. Go ahead.

510
00:25:12,933 --> 00:25:14,567
Go check on her, Mameng!

511
00:25:14,700 --> 00:25:16,533
- Why me?
- Go on.

512
00:25:16,667 --> 00:25:17,800
- Go ahead.
- Just check on her.

513
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:20,100
- But she has a gun!
- Just do it.

514
00:25:27,267 --> 00:25:29,300
[PHONE VIBRATES]

515
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:33,067
Hello, General Jacinto.
Good evening.

516
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:36,133
This evening is not good,
Domingo.

517
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:37,600
I have a problem.

518
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,933
My daughter, Sam, was ambushed.

519
00:25:40,767 --> 00:25:42,300
Only her car was found
in Soriano Street.

520
00:25:43,467 --> 00:25:46,100
I'll get my people
going at once, General.

521
00:25:46,233 --> 00:25:48,533
Look for my daughter.

522
00:25:48,667 --> 00:25:49,767
Yes, sir.

523
00:25:49,900 --> 00:25:54,300
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

524
00:25:54,433 --> 00:25:55,500
[GABO] Auntie!

525
00:25:55,633 --> 00:25:57,433
- Gabo.
- Here you go.

526
00:25:57,833 --> 00:26:00,067
You guys stay outside.

527
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:02,867
[MAMENG] I'll take care of her.

528
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:04,700
Come on, out.

529
00:26:04,833 --> 00:26:06,533
I'll treat her wounds.

530
00:26:06,667 --> 00:26:08,900
And I'll change
her clothes, too.

531
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:09,500
- Alright.
- Go on now.

532
00:26:09,633 --> 00:26:11,600
Let's stay outside.

533
00:26:20,933 --> 00:26:22,067
Who's that woman?

534
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:23,600
How did she get here?

535
00:26:23,933 --> 00:26:25,000
Well...

536
00:26:25,133 --> 00:26:26,867
she just fell through the roof.

537
00:26:27,367 --> 00:26:28,700
But why our roof?

538
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:32,100
Out of all the houses here,
why did she fall down ours?

539
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:35,800
Pa, could someone
be chasing her?

540
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,433
That's why she came
from the roof.

541
00:26:38,133 --> 00:26:40,067
Well, that's possible, too.

542
00:26:40,367 --> 00:26:42,233
If she's really being chased,

543
00:26:42,933 --> 00:26:45,033
then they might find
our house eventually.

544
00:26:45,167 --> 00:26:45,600
And our lives will be in danger.

545
00:26:45,733 --> 00:26:47,133
That's right.

546
00:26:47,567 --> 00:26:49,367
You should go outside, Dante.

547
00:26:50,033 --> 00:26:53,067
See if there are suspicious
looking people out there.

548
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,167
- Yeah, yeah. Alright.
- Go on.

549
00:26:54,300 --> 00:26:59,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

550
00:26:59,833 --> 00:27:00,667
Pa.

551
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:02,700
I hope nothing bad
happens to her.

552
00:27:02,833 --> 00:27:03,200
I hope so, too.

553
00:27:03,333 --> 00:27:09,300
[MUSIC SOFTENS]

554
00:27:14,167 --> 00:27:16,900
<i>I've already lost a child,
Ricardo!</i>

555
00:27:17,067 --> 00:27:20,867
<i> I can't lose another one!</i>

556
00:27:21,500 --> 00:27:24,467
<i>We should tell her family
where she is.</i>

557
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:26,900
They must be worried about her.

558
00:27:27,033 --> 00:27:28,533
<i>The Zafras
didn't just target Sam,</i>

559
00:27:28,667 --> 00:27:31,100
<i> but me, as well.</i>

560
00:27:32,033 --> 00:27:34,533
<i>Whatever they did
to my daughter,</i>

561
00:27:34,667 --> 00:27:36,833
I'll give back to them tenfold.

562
00:27:36,967 --> 00:27:40,733
<i>We'll give you anything
for Victor's freedom.</i>

563
00:27:40,867 --> 00:27:42,767
<i> 150 million.</i>

564
00:27:42,900 --> 00:27:43,933
<i>I'll do everything
you tell me to.</i>

565
00:27:44,067 --> 00:27:47,267
<i>There are armed men
walking around the area.</i>

566
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:49,633
<i>We won't stop
until we find that woman.</i>

567
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:51,733
<i> We should lock our doors.</i>

568
00:27:51,867 --> 00:27:55,200
<i>Those people might find out
where she is.</i>

569
00:27:55,333 --> 00:27:58,267
<i>They'll find out
we're hiding her in here.</i>

570
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,533
<i> Her life is in danger.</i>

571
00:27:59,667 --> 00:28:01,500
<i> We need to protect her.</i>

572
00:28:02,367 --> 00:28:09,267
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

573
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:12,200
Coco Martin's SiGabo!
